protocol_basis:
Byte-identical to a2t-direct-official-protocol except for the whitespace of the four system-prompt sentences. The released code has TWO spellings of the same prompt: the adapter's hard-coded default separates the sentences with single spaces (sha256 1c52cd2ebca6e4737b706ccc231b01f008d35276a2153000d74ec9500018258a), while configs/example_config.yaml carries them as a YAML block scalar -- newline-separated with a trailing newline (sha256 aa2e344ee52c59019b938926f37498e0dc9c80bd01f6521eba5c3d81309a491d) -- and run_benchmark.py passes that variant to the adapter whenever a config file is used. A config-driven official run therefore sends this variant. Both compose the same system message shape f"{system_prompt}

## Available Tools:
{tool_lines}", so this template differs from probes/r1_audio2tool_official.txt in whitespace alone (identical under str.split()); the trailing newline of the YAML scalar means three consecutive newlines separate the last sentence from the '## Available Tools:' header. Everything else -- the compact registry fill, the user turn (audio first, then the fixed sentence), the absence of a native tools list, the 256-token ceiling and greedy decoding -- is unchanged.
